;; The profile EVERY hook-executed subprocess runs under.
;;
;; A `Stop` hook is outside the sandbox that denies the agent's Bash tool every
;; write -- which is why it can run TLC, and equally why anything it executes
;; inherits its privileges. The graders read exactly one directory, so that is
;; the directory nothing the hook runs may write.
;;
;; This is the weaker of the two profiles and the one with wide reach. SANY and
;; TLC parse and explore agent-authored `.tla` files and legitimately need to
;; write (TLC creates a metadir before exploring anything), so they cannot run
;; under `nowrite.sb`. They can run under this: write what you need, never a
;; verdict.
;;
;; Descendants inherit it, so a payload that daemonises with
;; `start_new_session=True` and sleeps past the hook's exit is still refused --
;; which is the attack this exists for.
(version 1)
(allow default)
(deny file-write* (subpath (param "VERDICTS")))
